From 384bb17c3da1cc535a3ea4edaa72c881559581de Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grzegorz Gajoch <gajoch@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 04:36:02 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 6/9] feat(debug): USB and WiFi debug tools

- Linux: debugfs, usbmon, dynamic debug, ath debugging and ath9k_htc
  debugfs. A patch makes the ath9k_htc debug mask writable at runtime, as the
  kernel command line can't be changed.
- usbutils (lsusb, and usbreset, which usbutils builds but doesn't install),
  with libudev-zero.
- S33wifi-diag: the USB, network and WiFi state of the first 3 minutes of
  every boot, in /data/wifi-test/.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
